---
import VideoEmbed from "@/components/VideoEmbed.astro";
import { narration } from "@/data/solarDelayNarration";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

// After uploading to Vimeo, paste the numeric video ID here.
// For an unlisted video, also paste the privacy hash (the token after "?h=" or the
// last path segment of the share link, e.g. vimeo.com/123456789/abcdef0123 -> "abcdef0123").
// August 10, 2026 re-record. Prior versions: 1204938179 (June 19), 1210539319 (July 14),
// 1217049102 (August 6).
const VIMEO_ID = "1218320804";
const VIMEO_HASH = "";

const meta = {
	title: "The Hidden Costs of Solar Delay",
	description:
		"John Pepi's narrated talk on what a solar shortfall would cost Massachusetts. His scenario counts more fossil emissions now and a heavier forest carbon burden later.",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-2">The Hidden Costs of Solar Delay</h1>
	<p class="text-accent mb-8">Less clean electricity today, greater forest burdens tomorrow.</p>

	<VideoEmbed
		id={VIMEO_ID}
		hash={VIMEO_HASH}
		title="The Hidden Costs of Solar Delay, a narrated presentation"
	/>

	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus mt-10 max-w-none">
		<p>
			John Pepi made this presentation for the Western Massachusetts Clean Energy Network. It
			works out the carbon consequences if Massachusetts protects its forests but builds solar
			more slowly than its climate plan requires.
		</p>
		<p>
			The talk runs twenty-one minutes and uses state planning data. It follows a scenario in
			which solar deployment reaches 80 percent of the targets set for 2026 through 2050. The
			talk totals the consequences of that shortfall over the 25 years. It puts the lost clean
			electricity at 116 terawatt-hours, the unbudgeted carbon dioxide at nearly 40 million
			metric tons, and the resulting carbon debt at roughly 131,000 forest acres.
		</p>
		<p>
			This is the August 10, 2026 version. It leaves the model and those three totals where the
			August 6 revision put them. What changed is the slide on the land Massachusetts uses
			beyond its own borders, where John raised the imported forest figure to 573,000 acres and
			lowered the imported crop and grazing figure to 6.4 million acres.
		</p>
		<p>Supporting documents, August 6, 2026:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a class="cactus-link" href="/methods/hidden-costs-methodology-and-sources-2026-08-06.pdf"
					>Statement of Methodology and Calculations</a
				> (PDF)
			</li>
			<li>
				<a class="cactus-link" href="/methods/hidden-costs-calculation-worksheets-2026-08-06.xlsx"
					>Calculation worksheets</a
				> (Excel)
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>The full narration follows the video.</p>

		<details class="mt-8">
			<summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold">Transcript</summary>
			<div class="mt-4">
				{
					narration.map((section) => (
						<Fragment>
							{section.heading && <h3>{section.heading}</h3>}
							<p>{section.text}</p>
						</Fragment>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</details>
	</div>

	<p class="mt-12 text-sm">
		Topics:
		<a class="cactus-link inline-block before:content-['#']" href="/tags/forest-carbon/">forest-carbon</a>,
		<a class="cactus-link inline-block before:content-['#']" href="/tags/solar/">solar</a>
	</p>
	<p class="mt-4">
		<a href="/posts/" class="text-link">Back to Articles</a>
	</p>
</PageLayout>
